{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret","id":1166470,"title":"A small town with a dark secret...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-10T08:23:01-08:00","id":1166470,"title":"A small town with a dark secret...","content":"I\u2019m thinking of running a game in which a group of (human) PCs come to a town with a dark secret to investigate, Twin Peaks/Gravity Falls/X-Files style. Over time they\u2019ll come to know the place, and a cast of NPCs, and pick away at the central mystery. I plan to provide them with a corkboard to let them embrace their inner conspiracy theorists.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s incredibly unlikely they\u2019ll be looking here, but just in case\u2026 if you\u2019re in the Central Birmingham (UK) RPG club, please stop reading.<br /> <br /> So what\u2019s happening?<br /> <br /> The town is run by a demon Tempter ruling the town as a pocket kingdom and shaping it into their personal hell. The demon utilises several Covers as well as allies (human, Stigmatic, cultist and possibly even cryptid) to survey and control their little fiefdom. I\u2019m thinking they have three Covers from different social circles/strata; the Mayor (seldom seen, too busy/important and <i><i>obviously</i></i> a part of the conspiracy), a prominent citizen players regularly interact with (and hopefully come to trust) and someone quite innocuous (but a well-placed spy) like a homeless person or child.<br /> The PC investigators are, unknowingly, working for the Machine. Their investigation is for Its benefit and has a real chance of shredding the Tempter\u2019s Covers and destroying their life and the little Hell they\u2019ve built for themselves. They may actually be reporting to an angel.<br /> This setup allows for lots of reveals and nested truths that all lead to the biggest reveal of all; the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> I quite like the central idea but it naturally needs some flesh on its bones. I\u2019m thinking of having weird cryptid/cryptoflora stuff in the woods around the town and lots more God-Machine flavoured weirdness leaking out over the course of the investigation. I also want to flesh out the demon\u2019s human servants/cult. Are they dupes who serve the demon for power or protection? Somewhat aware of the supernatural world? A deeply religious cult devoted to a mythology the demon has built (or co-opted)?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m open to any ideas, but especially looking for different setups/motivations for the cult and general God-Machine weirdness to throw into the mix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T08:47:23-08:00","id":1166473,"title":"","content":"As usual when presented with multiple options, I ask: why not all of them? Either layered, in a Mystery Cult, or multiple &quot;competing&quot; organizations? If the Demon wants to maintain their control, why not own both the establishment and the opposition, the better to keep an eye on upstarts and using one to clean the other?<br /> <br /> Cryptoflora-wise, definitely have some Aether blocking type, and maybe a false positive emitter. The fun thing with distinctive Cryptoflora is that one the investigators figure out it's purpose, spotting it elsewhere bring all kinds of implications.<br /> <br /> Are you keeping this Demon/God-Machine only, or including other material as side notes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-10-2017, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T09:54:01-08:00","id":1166481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1166473#post1166473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As usual when presented with multiple options, I ask: why not all of them? Either layered, in a Mystery Cult, or multiple &quot;competing&quot; organizations? If the Demon wants to maintain their control, why not own both the establishment and the opposition, the better to keep an eye on upstarts and using one to clean the other?<br /> <br /> Cryptoflora-wise, definitely have some Aether blocking type, and maybe a false positive emitter. The fun thing with distinctive Cryptoflora is that one the investigators figure out it's purpose, spotting it elsewhere bring all kinds of implications.<br /> <br /> Are you keeping this Demon/God-Machine only, or including other material as side notes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was planning to keep it fairly pure, though if you've got an awesome idea by all means throw it out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T11:26:28-08:00","id":1166506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1166481#post1166481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was planning to keep it fairly pure, though if you've got an awesome idea by all means throw it out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing yet, though it does help to know what the options are when developing other plot hooks.<br /> <br /> Any key actors, scenes, plots, rumors, or locations decided yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T13:42:40-08:00","id":1166527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1166506#post1166506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing yet, though it does help to know what the options are when developing other plot hooks.<br /> <br /> Any key actors, scenes, plots, rumors, or locations decided yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actors - Besides the demon (and its Covers), nope. I think I'm more looking for hooks and factions over individuals, as I can conjure them pretty easily. I need locals who are actively part of the conspiracy (cults, individuals etc) but I want most residents to be either entirely unaware or the CofD 'unaware' (people who they know but recognise, possibly subconsciously, that the supernatural is best ignored.avoided and refuse to face up to it). <br /> <br /> Location could be isolated/rural, by the sea, an island (likely Scottish,as the game would be set in the UK).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T14:28:38-08:00","id":1166535,"title":"","content":"My first cult idea - the core of the cult are people helped, personally, by the demon. Through Pacts and other abilities, it took away their illnesses, their debts, their problems... They're indebted to it but also <i>grateful</i>. There's a genuine loyalty to the demon. This feeds nicely into the 'you're working for the real villain' reveal, though I do want to make the Tempter a bit more morally ambiguous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T15:02:17-08:00","id":1166542,"title":"","content":"A classic cult idea for this sort of setting is the one that defends the place from an outside threat. The sort of threat that can be kept at bay by following a set of rules, agreeing to accept sacrifices and pacts and keep an eye on those who are not part of it. You can personalize how much of the cult's mythology is a lie made up from the Demon and how much is based on standard CoD/GM's weirdness, past or present. It has not to be strictly supernatural, but even a mundane treat like a flood or generalized ruin might work.<br /> <br /> It's a tool of control, to make people both afraid and proud (perhaps a little self-righteous). The demon might pose as the &quot;inheritor of the secret knowledge that has protected the town for years&quot; that has the burden of making tough requests from time to time. Plenty of potential for various shenanigans, including the GM actually exploiting the cult beliefs to twist them against the demon (with the players as major tool for it to become possible)<br /> <br /> Some weirdness:<br /> - a hole in the ground, perfectly circular and whose walls are made of metal, can be found in the countryside, hidden under rocks/leaves/roots. Hot air and strange screeches sometimes comes out of it, but there's no end in sight.<br /> - Appearing at regular intervals and in different locations, what is essentially a holographic projection can be spotted around the place. It seems like a disturbed recording of people talking glossolalia and arguing. The characters are apparently naked, but they're featureless, androgynous blanks. They wield tools and weapons who seem at the same time ancient and futuristic. The recordings are many and each one is different, but still limited in amount. Sometimes the characters flicker for a second and it seems as if they can see those watching them.<br /> - Every morning, at 4:44 AM, a frog drops from the sky and hits the ground. The fall does not hurt it.<br /> - Bring a old radio to the top of a nearby hill, hit the right frequence and you'll be able to hear a radio host speaking in stereotypical 50s tone making a brief prediction of the way you're gonna die. There's a little urban legend about this, with people daring each other to try. Most just don't find the frequence, but some do.<br /> - For a maritime setting: a little boat is sailing away from the coast. Seems like an ordinary one, except for its crab-like legs made of rusted iron, steel and glass which can only be spotted from nearby while underwater. Sometimes, at night, the boat comes to land and hunts.<br /> <br /> Can make up some more, if you think you could use those. I always have fun writing this sort of weird tidbits, but I'm not sure if that's what you're looking for","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 12-10-2017, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T15:20:23-08:00","id":1166548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1166542#post1166542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A classic cult idea for this sort of setting is the one that defends the place from an outside threat. The sort of threat that can be kept at bay by following a set of rules, agreeing to accept sacrifices and pacts and keep an eye on those who are not part of it. You can personalize how much of the cult's mythology is a lie made up from the Demon and how much is based on standard CoD/GM's weirdness, past or present. It has not to be strictly supernatural, but even a mundane treat like a flood or generalized ruin might work.<br /> <br /> It's a tool of control, to make people both afraid and proud (perhaps a little self-righteous). The demon might pose as the &quot;inheritor of the secret knowledge that has protected the town for years&quot; that has the burden of making tough requests from time to time. Plenty of potential for various shenanigans, including the GM actually exploiting the cult beliefs to twist them against the demon (with the players as major tool for it to become possible)</div> </div> </div> </div>I quite like this... as it can easily be combined with suborned Infrastructure ( once operated/protected/attended/etc by human cultists). This town was built around some Infrastructure. Perhaps this fell into disuse at some point and the demon moved to reactivate it (or just took it over), creating/subverting a cult and using the Infrastructure as an Aether supply. <br /> <br /> Now the Machine wants to reactivate it, or has just noticed something hacked Its dormant Infrastructure and wants to move back in....<br /> <br /> I could even have the Machine's ultimate aim actively destructive for the town and centered on said Infrastructure... The weird rituals to keep disaster at bay? Entirely necessary. But that might be a bit too cheap.<br /> <br /> Some good quality weirdness there too. Feel free to add more. <br /> <br /> This is already going well. Thank you both.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T16:17:37-08:00","id":1166558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1166548#post1166548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is already going well. Thank you both.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't mention it. It is my favorite kind of setting so helping comes easier for me this time around. Glad to be useful.<br /> <br /> I'll think about some more weird phenomena and creatures as well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T16:53:27-08:00","id":1166568,"title":"","content":"Cryptid ideas:<br /> Mermaids (human base, Aquatic Form Ability, various Vocal Embeds optional)<br /> Loch Ness Monster (time displaced plesiosaur?). For some fun, make it a good conversationalist.<br /> Bogle (small mischievous troublemakers with Cacophonic Embeds and a Ban/Glitch that prevents them from harming those who obey their parents).<br /> <br /> Rumors<br /> The Milkman delivers fresh milk every 4th day of the week... despite the dairy having gone under decades ago. The milk is always fresh (*always* even if left open for days it never spoils). The bottles always vanish before the next delivery, always whenever no one is looking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T01:09:06-08:00","id":1166652,"title":"","content":"So I've given some thoughts to the location and, building on the idea that the town is built around some piece of Infrastructure that could destroy it, I thought of Centralia (Pennsylvania) and the fire raging underground. For those unaware, the fire raged for years and life on the surface was mostly unchanged (besides the occasional plume of toxic gas, cracking pavements, sinkholes and subsidence). Britain has a coal mining history and many former mining towns (mostly in the Midlands, North and Wales), many of which have suffered decline since coal mining stopped after the Thatcher government.<br /> <br /> Perhaps our town is a rare exception, a town that is blossoming (somehow), but beneath the town there is a network of tunnels and mines, some hiding ancient Infrastructure and some aflame, the fires held back by suborned Infrastructure, the demon's influence and the refusal of townspeople to accept the truth. One of the first mysteries, and the most mundane, is that many townspeople are fully aware of the underground fire and keep it secret (perhaps it threatens a tourist industry... or something...)<br /> <br /> This adds some pretty fun locations; the mines themselves, for one. I also can't help but think of a real pub (The Crooked House) I've been to in a heavily mined area which has partly subsided, with the floors of different rooms tilting in different directions.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm wondering about an oracle at Delphi style oracular tradition based around toxic gas, but that might be a bit too odd...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 12-11-2017, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T11:33:06-08:00","id":1166751,"title":"","content":"What about instead of toxic gas, it is ground-based magnetic currents? Scotland is lousy with various divination methods, so you have your pick.<br /> <br /> This is more a plug-in-play idea, since it doesn't really tie into anything necessarily, but what about a place/ritual/circumstance that send people on a nice Astral voyage? Nothing quite like a psychedelic dream journey to kadath for a non-sequiteur to eat time or drop hints.<br /> <br /> Is there anyone in town who &quot;knows&quot; (they know stuff is going on, but who they think is responsible and why may be of varying accuracy) but isn't G-M backed or allied with the Demon? Knowledgeable librarian, crazy hermit, cab driver?<br /> <br /> So, mining town, eh? Molemen Cryptids? Delving Too Deep? Hmm, throw in an Earthbound (Idigam, or Descent take on the Fallen concept)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-11-2017, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T02:30:29-08:00","id":1166937,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m presently looking into various local superstitions in the different mining areas to, uh, <i>mine</i> for ideas for cryptids and things. Knockers/imps are an obvious one (and feel like Imperatives to me), but as much of the game won\u2019t be underground I\u2019m looking for more terrestrial things. I\u2019m also considering that the Aether comes from the ground in \u2018vents\u2019 creating a bizarre cryptid ecosystem almost like the geothermic vents in the abyss\u2026<br /> <br /> Currently I\u2019m considering splitting the cult in two.<br /> <br /> The local cult \u2013 Primarily devoted to the appeasing of the (suborned) Infrastructure and hiding the truth, though they have strange rituals (some of them holdovers from mining traditions/superstitions). The demon joined and essentially took over this cult, twisting its practises to suit their Aether harvesting and their idea of the town as their fiefdom.<br /> <br /> The demon\u2019s cult \u2013 In truth, these are not a cult. They are not organised and many are unaware of each other. They consider of cadre of people personally helped by the demon through Pacts and other supernatural abilities. The demon took away their pain, removed their debts and other problems. Some are part of the town\u2019s cult but most are not. They are the demon\u2019s eyes, ears and (if need be) catspaws.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>. There will be a few potential clue sources and allies who know bits and pieces. I\u2019m half tempted to have a former cultist of the old town cult who never signed on to the new cult or essentially retired from the cult (probably an old miner). Depending on what set off the investigation (which I\u2019ll talk about shortly) there will be locals with information willing or even desperate to help. One clue will be local people complaining about potholes (despite the fact investigators can see they\u2019re constantly being repaired), the most British clue imaginable.<br /> <br /> Currently I\u2019m considering where local cult needs agents to pull off the cover-up. The council, the people who fix the potholes, local emergency services, local press\u2026 Any other obvious places I\u2019ve missed?<br /> <br /> Just as important\u2026 What set off the investigation? Deaths? Disappearances? Tax irregularities? The cover story doesn\u2019t need to be true, as the investigation is the Machine\u2019s tool. I am tempted by the classic mysterious deaths/disappearances (shades of the Wicker Man creeping in\u2026) but perhaps that\u2019s too clich\u00e9. I do want the local cult and demon a bit more morally ambiguous as currently the demon is holding back the destruction of the town and served by people it has personally helped. It needs a little bit of a dark side (without going fully evil).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also wondering about the function of the Infrastructure, though to be fair that probably doesn\u2019t ever need to be explained. Is it coal powered and the mine partly existed just to fuel it? Did the deaths of miners turns Its gears, perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 12-12-2017, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T05:02:21-08:00","id":1166952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1166652#post1166652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've given some thoughts to the location and, building on the idea that the town is built around some piece of Infrastructure that could destroy it, I thought of Centralia (Pennsylvania) and the fire raging underground. For those unaware, the fire raged for years and life on the surface was mostly unchanged (besides the occasional plume of toxic gas, cracking pavements, sinkholes and subsidence). Britain has a coal mining history and many former mining towns (mostly in the Midlands, North and Wales), many of which have suffered decline since coal mining stopped after the Thatcher government.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. You can have things like walls of flames being kept at bay by invisible forces, bizarre structures and stuff like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1166652#post1166652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I'm wondering about an oracle at Delphi style oracular tradition based around toxic gas, but that might be a bit too odd...</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. If you feel that way, you can always reframe it as something less ancient and respected. The casual, kinda sketchy, answer to Delphi: a crazy man/woman living on the outskirts of town who inhales gas and is said to predict the future. I'm thinking less of temple, attendants, holy cave and offerings to Apollo and more of shack, flea-ridden dog, hole in the ground covered by a plate of iron and beer and cigarettes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1166937#post1166937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m presently looking into various local superstitions in the different mining areas to, uh, <i>mine</i> for ideas for cryptids and things. Knockers/imps are an obvious one (and feel like Imperatives to me), but as much of the game won\u2019t be underground I\u2019m looking for more terrestrial things. I\u2019m also considering that the Aether comes from the ground in \u2018vents\u2019 creating a bizarre cryptid ecosystem almost like the geothermic vents in the abyss\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. I know a couple of mining legends from my country, but overall they tend to have the same theme all around the world: you get down there and you never know what you can unearth, plus there's always the chance for a door to Underworld/Hell to open. Also, that those who die into mines without proper burial don't rest and that their families and sons are bad luck, to the point they're basically doomed to end the same way if they work in the mines as well. Speaking of other things, I've always been a fan of banshees, so I humbly suggest a GM take on those. The ecosystem aspect sounds really cool to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1166652#post1166652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently I\u2019m considering where local cult needs agents to pull off the cover-up. The council, the people who fix the potholes, local emergency services, local press\u2026 Any other obvious places I\u2019ve missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're good. If the town is isolated from the world, you got it covered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1166652#post1166652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as important\u2026 What set off the investigation? Deaths? Disappearances? Tax irregularities? The cover story doesn\u2019t need to be true, as the investigation is the Machine\u2019s tool. I am tempted by the classic mysterious deaths/disappearances (shades of the Wicker Man creeping in\u2026) but perhaps that\u2019s too clich\u00e9. I do want the local cult and demon a bit more morally ambiguous as currently the demon is holding back the destruction of the town and served by people it has personally helped. It needs a little bit of a dark side (without going fully evil).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll throw in the &quot;insurance/speculation&quot; option. Either someone saws potential gain in the town and wants to acquire lands and permits to begin the works and sends the players to check everything is in order and persuade the locals to sign, or someone <i>does not</i> want to spend money and asks the players to find a good reasons not to. After all, the town is little and distant: a scam is far too easy to pull off and deserves further investigation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1166652#post1166652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m also wondering about the function of the Infrastructure, though to be fair that probably doesn\u2019t ever need to be explained. Is it coal powered and the mine partly existed just to fuel it? Did the deaths of miners turns Its gears, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, why not? Another one is that there was something to be found down there which needed other kinds of Infrastructure to be sent away and, whether because the resource became rarer or the complementary Infrastructure had issues, the GM did not allocate further forces to keep the operation going or rework it into something different. Until now, of course","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 12-12-2017, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T04:44:50-08:00","id":1167265,"title":"","content":"Well, for a &quot;dark side&quot; to the Demon, they could have done dramatic and potentially disproportionate actions in pursuit of keeping their Cover or the town secure. I've found that the interests of security can easily push Unchained into desperate actions. Possible understandable, considering what they are hiding from, but that's hard to sell to the people adversely affected.<br /> <br /> Want them &quot;bad&quot;? Accentuate what they've done. Want them sympathetic? Accentuate why they felt they had to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T13:23:00-08:00","id":1167759,"title":"","content":"I think there is a potential good use of a time Splinter here, having the PCs end up back in the town before the Demon dealing with the original Cult and Infrastructure could help show the goods and bads of the Demon's version of the town by contrast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T14:17:10-08:00","id":1168022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1167759#post1167759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is a potential good use of a time Splinter here, having the PCs end up back in the town before the Demon dealing with the original Cult and Infrastructure could help show the goods and bads of the Demon's version of the town by contrast.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty great idea. Also I could use Splinters to explore possible (fiery) futures...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T14:36:19-08:00","id":1168024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1168022#post1168022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a pretty great idea. Also I could use Splinters to explore possible (fiery) futures...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then leave them wondering if that future is caused by them stopping the Demon or helping them...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T21:56:11-08:00","id":1169572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret#post1166470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m thinking they have three Covers from different social circles/strata; the Mayor (seldom seen, too busy/important and <i><i>obviously</i></i> a part of the conspiracy), a prominent citizen players regularly interact with (and hopefully come to trust) and someone quite innocuous (but a well-placed spy) like a homeless person or child.</div> </div> </div> </div>The covers:<br /> The mayor. Recommend the mayor's secretary. A good secretary can control access to who gets to see the mayor, and what the mayor in turn gets to see, while being nearly invisible, the person at the front desk is just so much furniture, right? Also, politicians come and go, but career civil service is in the ground floor for life.<br /> <br /> The prominent citizen. Recommend the town grocery store owner. (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JgJt4sArUHI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JgJt4sArUHI</a>). If the community is small enough, they might be the only game in town. In addition to be a major nerve center for town gossip, the owner is also in a position to get what people need (&quot;Yes, Ms. Thompson, I understand that times are tough, tell you what, I think we can fudge today's bill in exchange for a small favor&quot;)<br /> <br /> The innocuous. Possible choices include a local veteran, or a disowned LGBT youth forced out onto the streets. Both can disappear from and reappear in town without arousing suspicion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T23:01:59-08:00","id":1170869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1166548#post1166548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I quite like this... as it can easily be combined with suborned Infrastructure ( once operated/protected/attended/etc by human cultists). This town was built around some Infrastructure. Perhaps this fell into disuse at some point and the demon moved to reactivate it (or just took it over), creating/subverting a cult and using the Infrastructure as an Aether supply.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like this theme. The remnants of abandoned factories and stores dotting the landscape, leaving desolated communities in their wake, reflects the G-M's habit of starting projects, abandoning them, and then repurposing them without regard to anyone caught in It\u2019s way.<br /> <br /> Sources to mine:<br /> <br /> Jan Harold Brunvald has written a number of works about urban legends and American folklore, it sounds like you\u2019re using a UK location, but there\u2019s still good material<br /> <br /> UFO Crash at Roswell: Genesis of a Modern Myth by Benson Saler<br /> <br /> Methland: The Death and Life of an American Small Town by Nick Reding<br /> <br /> RPGs: Heaven and Earth is an old series by Abstract Nova Press, it has a small-town Weirdness setting with theistic horror theme.<br /> <br /> The Esoterrorists by Pelgrane, is more developed around an eeeevil cult, but it does have a nice, modular town that you can pull apart for details<br /> <br /> Podcasts: Welcome to Nightvale<br /> <br /> The Black Tapes<br /> <br /> Someone Knows Something - Nonfiction, very good.<br /> <br /> King Falls AM<br /> <br /> The Ozarks Explained<br /> <br /> <br /> Suggested locals:<br /> <br /> The Abandoned Airfield. I guarantee you, this will get your players attention. Doesn't matter what kind of clues you put there, the words Abandoned Airfield will draw them like like flies to honey. Could be a pilot\u2019s logbook with UFO sightings, could be the remains of an old smuggling operation cargo, could be an active smuggling operation with modern tech (drones, ultra-light cesna aircraft)<br /> <br /> The Local military installation. Is your small town dependent on a military base for economic viability? How do the locals feel about it?<br /> <br /> Third generation legal practice. Lawyers/solicitors can effectively become local aristocracy, potentially making their mark in local politics. If a particular law firm has operated across multiple generations, it likely has rooms full of old files that aren\u2019t digitally stored, possibly going back before the town's founding. Good place to investigate land/property transfers, odd deaths, etc.<br /> <br /> The town recreation centers. Look, even cultist like ice skating, or bowling, or eating frozen yogurt.<br /> <br /> The remains of other supernatural societies. Despite the whole idea of supernatural societies dating back to Atlantis/father wolf/the dark mother/ whatever, my view of supernatural groups is that they\u2019re more like street gangs or role-playing groups: the come together, they last a while, then they dissipate. Finding out that your town once had a group of supernatural protectors (or overlords) that just <i>moved on</i> with their lives can be a poignant statement on the eventual fate small town they once protected\u2026 and then there\u2019s any supernatural threats they might have left behind, unattended. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T18:30:31-08:00","id":1173655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1169572#post1169572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The covers:<br /> The mayor. Recommend the mayor's secretary. A good secretary can control access to who gets to see the mayor, and what the mayor in turn gets to see, while being nearly invisible, the person at the front desk is just so much furniture, right? Also, politicians come and go, but career civil service is in the ground floor for life.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Running with this for sure. Thanks for all the suggestions!<br /> <br /> The town is currently bordering a forest.There are cryptids in the woods, of course, though I'm still debating what they are (owls, deer, foxes?). I do know the cryptid Aether-ecosystem is based around vents of Aether-rich toxic gas.<br /> <br /> A major landmark is a Manor House turned hotel that regularlyhosts weddings. The family that built it were beneficiaries of the mining operations and God-Machine cultists. I'm tempted to have a few weird objects in the Hotel, things that slipped under the radar... Might raid the SCP foundation for ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T05:07:52-08:00","id":1173737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1173655#post1173655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running with this for sure. Thanks for all the suggestions!</div> </div> </div> </div>The mayor could be in their position due to a Pact. Or be completely ignorant, if you want the &quot;Mayor is a Demon&quot; as a Red(-ish) Herring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1173655#post1173655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The town is currently bordering a forest.There are cryptids in the woods, of course, though I'm still debating what they are (owls, deer, foxes?). I do know the cryptid Aether-ecosystem is based around vents of Aether-rich toxic gas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Owls. Bears. Owlbears! Though considering the source of the Aether is underground, den or burrowing animals might work best. That even might be another clue, if the only Crytpids encountered are animals that live underground.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1173655#post1173655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A major landmark is a Manor House turned hotel that regularlyhosts weddings. The family that built it were beneficiaries of the mining operations and God-Machine cultists. I'm tempted to have a few weird objects in the Hotel, things that slipped under the radar... Might raid the SCP foundation for ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manor you say? Weddings? Sounds perfect for being host to a ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T13:53:17-08:00","id":1173831,"title":"","content":"Annoyingly, there is no Mayor in a small, rural British town. The government will be a mix of various councils (the bureaucratic mess is one the demon, a midranking civil servant in the council structure) keeps things under wraps.<br /> <br /> Your suggestion about burrowing animals is an <i>excellent</i> one.I do have an image in my head of a deer shedding its velvet to reveal metal antlers, though... <br /> <br /> I've got friends on board to roleplay a phone conversation, actually. I'm considering phone calls from angels/demons/ghosts/Imperatives (Imps might not be smart enough technically) or something weirder like the sentient fear-powered phone from that one mage book. A sentient aether-powered phone, perhaps..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T15:13:01-08:00","id":1173852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1173831#post1173831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Annoyingly, there is no Mayor in a small, rural British town. The government will be a mix of various councils (the bureaucratic mess is one the demon, a midranking civil servant in the council structure) keeps things under wraps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those British. Turning even the simple job of Provincial Rul- I mean Mayor, into a committee activity.<br /> <br /> Still, some of the members of the councils could have gotten their positions via Pact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1173831#post1173831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your suggestion about burrowing animals is an <i>excellent</i> one.I do have an image in my head of a deer shedding its velvet to reveal metal antlers, though...</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the image of those horns also serving as either Jacob's Ladders, or pipe organs (bring your ominous gothic music with you!). Maybe a one-of?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1166470-a-small-town-with-a-dark-secret?p=1173831#post1173831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got friends on board to roleplay a phone conversation, actually. I'm considering phone calls from angels/demons/ghosts/Imperatives (Imps might not be smart enough technically) or something weirder like the sentient fear-powered phone from that one mage book. A sentient aether-powered phone, perhaps..</div> </div> </div> </div>Lares? Or if you are using time splinters, maybe calls from someone in another timeline?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T17:19:49-08:00","id":1173877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.